---Resetting the channel can help to clear errors from misconfigurations in the encoder. A reset refreshes the ingest stream and removes previous content.
---
---`POST /channelGroup/{ChannelGroupName}/channel/{ChannelName}/reset`
---Errors: AccessDeniedException, ConflictException, InternalServerException, ResourceNotFoundException, ThrottlingException, ValidationException.
---@param input aws.mediapackagev2.ResetChannelStateRequest
---@return aws.mediapackagev2.ResetChannelStateResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:reset_channel_state(input) end

---Resetting the origin endpoint can help to resolve unexpected behavior and other content packaging issues. It also helps to preserve special events when you don't want the previous content to be available for viewing. A reset clears out all previous content from the origin endpoint.
---
---`POST /channelGroup/{ChannelGroupName}/channel/{ChannelName}/originEndpoint/{OriginEndpointName}/reset`
---Errors: AccessDeniedException, ConflictException, InternalServerException, ResourceNotFoundException, ThrottlingException, ValidationException.
---@param input aws.mediapackagev2.ResetOriginEndpointStateRequest
---@return aws.mediapackagev2.ResetOriginEndpointStateResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
